[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:15. Good News]
[00:00.260] Passage 15 | 文章十五
[00:02.465] Good news. | 佳音。
[00:05.270] The secretary told me that Mr. Harmsworth would see me. | 秘书告诉我哈姆斯沃思先生会接见我。
[00:10.560] I felt very nervous when I went into his office. | 我走进他的办公室时，感到非常紧张。
[00:14.780] He did not look up from his desk when I entered. | 我进去时，他没有从办公桌上抬起头。
[00:19.040] After I had sat down, he said that business was very bad. | 我坐下后，他说生意非常不好。
[00:24.885] He told me that the firm could not afford to pay such large salaries. | 他告诉我，公司付不起这么高的薪水。
[00:29.960] 20 people had already left. | 已经有20人离开了。
[00:33.450] I knew that my turn had come. | 我知道轮到我了。
[00:37.755] Mr. Harmsworth, I said in a weak voice.| 哈姆斯沃思先生，我用微弱的声音说道。
[00:42.290] Don't interrupt, he said.| 不要打断我的话，他说。
[00:45.350] Then he smiled | 然后他笑了，
[00:48.380] and told me I would receive an extra 100 pounds a year.| 并告诉我，我会额外获得每年100英镑。